# 01 — PRESENTATION DESIGN PRINCIPLES

## Overview

The first activity focused on applying presentation and visual design principles to create effective promotional material.

For this activity, I created a promotional poster for **Arrupe Hall Booth VI**, featuring a coffee-themed concept. The poster promotes the message:

> **"Free coffee. No Catch. Just caffeine and good vibes."**

The purpose of the design was to create an eye-catching, visually organized poster that could easily convey the event, promotion, location, and date to the audience.

Instead of simply placing text and images together, I carefully considered the arrangement, typography, visual elements, and overall composition to make the design more appealing and easier to understand.

---

## My Concept

The concept of my design centers on **coffee, relaxation, and good vibes**.

I used coffee-related elements, such as a latte, coffee beans, and coffee leaves, to immediately establish the poster's theme. The large coffee cup is one of the main visual elements and helps capture the audience's attention.

The overall design uses a warm and neutral background that complements the coffee theme. The combination of brown, cream, black, and green tones creates a natural and cozy atmosphere.

I also included an illustrated figure holding a coffee cup to add personality and visual interest to the poster. This helps make the promotional material feel more engaging and connected to the student community.

The main goal of the design was to communicate the event information while maintaining a creative, warm, and visually balanced composition.

---

## Design Principles I Applied

### 1. Visual Hierarchy

Visual hierarchy was applied by organizing the elements according to their importance.

The coffee cup and the title **"ARRUPE HALL BOOTH VI"** are among the first elements that catch the viewer's attention. The large typography helps emphasize the location and booth number.

The promotional message:

> **"Free coffee. No Catch. Just caffeine and good vibes."**

is placed below the main title, allowing the audience to understand the purpose of the booth after identifying the main subject.

The date is also highlighted inside a dark, rounded shape to make it easy to notice.

This hierarchy helps guide the viewer's attention from the main visual to the booth information, promotion, and event date.

---

### 2. Contrast

Contrast was used to make important information stand out from the background.

The dark typography contrasts with the light and textured background, making the text easier to read.

The dark date label also creates a strong visual contrast against the lighter background. This helps separate the date from the other elements and makes it easier for the audience to identify.

The brown tones of the coffee and coffee beans also contrast with the cream-colored background, strengthening the coffee theme and creating visual interest.

---

### 3. Alignment

Alignment was used to organize the text and visual elements throughout the poster.

The main title, promotional message, and date are positioned on the left side, creating a clear information section. Meanwhile, the illustrated figure is positioned on the right side to create visual balance.

The text elements follow a structured arrangement, preventing the poster from looking random or disorganized.

Proper alignment helped create a cleaner composition and made the information easier to follow.

---

### 4. Balance

Balance was an important principle in the overall composition.

The large coffee cup is positioned at the upper portion of the design, while the illustrated figure occupies the right side. The text is placed primarily on the left side.

These elements help balance one another and prevent one area of the poster from feeling too empty or too crowded.

The coffee beans and leaves were also placed around the composition as supporting elements. These smaller details help fill empty spaces without taking attention away from the main message.

---

### 5. Emphasis

Emphasis was used to highlight the most important elements of the promotional poster.

The large coffee cup immediately establishes the design's main theme. The title **"ARRUPE HALL BOOTH VI"** is also emphasized through its large font size.

The message about free coffee is another important point, so it is placed prominently below the title.

The date is given additional emphasis by placing it inside a dark rounded shape.

These design choices ensure that viewers can quickly identify the most important information.

---

### 6. Repetition and Consistency

Consistency was maintained through the repeated use of coffee-related visual elements.

The coffee cup, coffee beans, and leaves all support the same theme. The warm and earthy color palette is also repeated throughout the design.

Typography is used consistently to maintain a unified appearance. Although different font sizes are used to establish hierarchy, the overall style remains visually connected.

This consistency helps make the poster feel like a single, unified design.

---

### 7. Proximity

Proximity was used to group related information together.

The main title, promotional message, and date are positioned close enough to show that they are all connected to the same event.

The coffee-related visual elements are also grouped around the composition to reinforce the overall theme.

By placing related elements near one another, the design becomes easier to understand and visually organized.

---

### 8. Simplicity

Although the poster contains several visual elements, I avoided adding unnecessary information.

The design focuses mainly on the booth name, promotional message, date, and coffee-themed visuals.

The background remains simple enough to support the content without distracting from the important information.

Applying simplicity helped maintain readability and ensured the audience could easily understand the poster's purpose.

---

## How I Developed the Final Output

The development process began by identifying the promotional poster's main purpose.

I first considered the key information to include, such as the booth name, promotion, and date.

After organizing the information, I developed a coffee-themed concept that would align with the idea of offering free coffee and fostering a positive atmosphere.

I then arranged the major visual elements, including the coffee cup and illustrated figure. After establishing the main composition, I added the title, promotional message, and date.

Coffee beans and leaves were added as supporting elements to strengthen the theme and fill the composition.

Finally, I reviewed the arrangement of the elements and adjusted the spacing, hierarchy, and balance to ensure that the design remained visually organized and easy to understand.

---

## How the Design Principles Improved My Presentation

Applying design principles improved the overall effectiveness of my design.

**Visual hierarchy** helped direct the audience toward the most important information.

**Contrast** improved the readability of the text and helped important elements stand out.

**Alignment and proximity** organized the information and made the layout easier to understand.

**Balance** prevented the design from appearing too crowded on one side.

**Consistency and repetition** strengthened the coffee theme and created a unified visual identity.

Finally, **simplicity** ensured that the design communicated its message without overwhelming the audience with unnecessary information.

By applying these principles, the final output became more visually appealing, organized, readable, and effective as a promotional poster.

---

## What I Learned

This activity taught me that effective design is not only about making a poster visually attractive.

Every design element should have a purpose and contribute to the communication of the message.

I learned how principles such as hierarchy, contrast, alignment, balance, consistency, proximity, and simplicity can improve the way information is presented.

I also learned that visual elements and typography should work together to guide the audience's attention.

Most importantly, I learned that a well-designed presentation or promotional material should make information easier to understand while also creating a visually engaging experience.

